# examples/games/07_platformer, played: the world to the flag and a best run
# kept, then three falls, game over, and the title showing the best run. On
# the way, the pause: the HUD's button, Enter, and Escape both ways.
#
# Right and left run (the arrows), Space jumps. The levels are three in a row
# in one LDtk world, and walking off the right edge of one is a change to the
# next. The moves were recorded from tests/platformer_play.cpp's bot -- the
# same route, through the Desert's key and door -- played under this driver;
# nothing in the game is random. See tests/e2e/script.h for the grammar.

# --- the title -----------------------------------------------------------------

1 shot title
4 expect scene TitleScene
# Play has the focus: Enter alone starts a run.
5 tap KEY_ENTER
5 expect scene LevelScene

# --- the happy path: the flag ---------------------------------------------------

# The Meadow: right, and over what is in the way.
6 press KEY_RIGHT
84 tap KEY_SPACE
# Space jumps, and does not press the HUD's Pause button, as it would the
# focused button of a menu: the player reads Space, so the level is being
# played, and a HUD over a game being played takes no focus by itself.
84 expect scene LevelScene
170 tap KEY_SPACE
222 tap KEY_SPACE
# Off its right edge and into the Desert, a scene of its own.
331 expect scene LevelScene
# Wait for the moving platform, ride it, and up to the key above it.
404 tap KEY_SPACE
447 release KEY_RIGHT
731 press KEY_RIGHT
755 tap KEY_SPACE
784 tap KEY_SPACE
813 release KEY_RIGHT
813 press KEY_LEFT
830 tap KEY_SPACE
858 press KEY_RIGHT
858 release KEY_LEFT
860 shot key_taken
873 tap KEY_SPACE
# The key's door, opened by walking into it.
930 shot door_open
# The Snowfield, where a bat costs a life on the way up to the flag.
958 expect scene LevelScene
994 tap KEY_SPACE
1038 tap KEY_SPACE
1083 tap KEY_SPACE
1155 release KEY_RIGHT
1213 press KEY_RIGHT
1411 tap KEY_SPACE
1455 tap KEY_SPACE
1497 tap KEY_SPACE
1541 expect scene LevelScene
1542 expect scene EndScene
# Nine coins in 25.6 s, and the first run is a new best, kept with rmp::save.
1545 shot you_made_it

# Play again: the first button has the focus. A new run, from the Meadow.
1550 release KEY_RIGHT
1555 tap KEY_ENTER
1555 expect scene LevelScene

# --- the pause -------------------------------------------------------------------

# The HUD's Pause button, for a finger, which is the one way a phone has. A
# button fires on the way up, the frame after the click. The level freezes
# behind the menu, clock and all: blurred where there is a GPU, and only dimmed
# here, under raylib's software renderer.
1560 click 730 42
1560 expect scene LevelScene
1561 expect scene PauseScene
1564 shot paused
# Resume has the focus, whatever the pointer did: Enter resumes.
1566 tap KEY_ENTER
1566 expect scene LevelScene
# Escape pauses, and Escape resumes.
1569 tap KEY_ESCAPE
1569 expect scene PauseScene
1572 tap KEY_ESCAPE
1572 expect scene LevelScene

# --- the failure path: three falls ------------------------------------------------

# Straight into the Meadow's first pit, three times: a life lost each, and
# back to the start.
1574 press KEY_RIGHT
1906 expect scene LevelScene
1907 expect scene EndScene
1910 shot game_over

# Menu, the second button: down, then Enter. The title reads the best run back.
1913 release KEY_RIGHT
1915 tap KEY_DOWN
1918 tap KEY_ENTER
1918 expect scene TitleScene
1921 shot title_with_best
1921 end
